## Slash Commands (In-Session) — Quick Reference

For the authoritative list, run `/help` in-session or see `references/slash-commands-reference.md` for the full registry. The most commonly used:

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `/new` or `/reset` | Fresh session |
| `/clear` | Clear screen + new session (CLI) |
| `/retry` | Resend last message |
| `/undo` | Remove last exchange |
| `/compress` | Manually compress context |
| `/model [name]` | Show or change model |
| `/reasoning [level]` | Set reasoning effort (none|minimal|low|medium|high|xhigh) |
| `/personality [name]` | Set personality |
| `/skill <name>` | Load a skill into session |
| `/reload-skills` | Re-scan for added/removed skills |
| `/cron` | Manage cron jobs |
| `/curator [sub]` | Background skill maintenance |
| `/kanban [sub]` | Multi-profile work board |
| `/usage` | Token usage |
| `/status` | Session info (gateway) |
| `/help` | Show all commands |
| `/quit` | Exit CLI |

The registry of record is `hermes_cli/commands.py` — every consumer (autocomplete, Telegram menu, Slack mapping, `/help`) derives from it.

