## Local Agent Personality Prototyping

When the user is exploring stylized agent personalities (e.g., historical, philosophical, or eccentric voices), treat the first several turns as pure clarification. The user frequently signals exploratory thinking with phrases such as "just some thoughts" or explicit pushback ("NO"). Do not propose implementation, VPS moves, scripts, or cronjobs until the personality voice, interaction medium, and text-feeding workflow are explicitly confirmed.

Preferred local workflow for this class of task:
1. Define the target voice and constraints in plain terms.
2. Confirm interaction surface (terminal first, Telegram later).
3. Confirm text ingestion method (local files fed on demand).
4. Only then move to system prompt drafting or retrieval setup.

This user strongly prefers local-first validation before any always-on infrastructure. Encode this preference into every personality-related conversation until the user explicitly requests the VPS transition.
